## Decisions

The rows answer CannObserv/broker#22's design questions. "As the core" adopts its answer unchanged; otherwise say what <REPO> does, and which pilot it follows.

| # | Question | Decision |
|---|---|---|
| D1 | Location and ownership | As the core: `/srv/<REPO>`, releases owned by root. Service user: `exedev` to start, dedicated user as follow-up <FOLLOW_UP> |
| D2 | Atomicity and rollback | As the core: `releases/<sha12>`, a link switched by `rename(2)`; a rollback is a deploy of the older build. `KEEP`: |
| D3 | Git source | As the core: `git fetch` in the checkout; only a commit on `origin/main` deploys to live |
| D4 | Who deploys, and how | As the core: `scripts/deploy.sh` from the checkout, as the deploy user, `sudo -n` where it must; `.skills/deploy_command` names it |
| D5 | Dependencies and private wheels | `uv sync --locked` per release; private index: |
| D6 | Env and state | `/etc/<REPO>/` only; written paths moved to: |
| D7 | Restart semantics | As the core: each enabled long-running unit restarted when live moves, drained by its `TimeoutStopSec=`; timers never forced. Restart window: |
| D8 | Guards, relocated | The main-checkout guard is deleted; integrity checks move to `post_build_check`: |
| D9 | Build id and drift | `REVISION`, reported by: ; drift check: a follow-up |
| D10 | Failure visibility | `OnFailure=` handlers: |
| D11 | Dev services on the host | `DEV_TARGET`: none / a dev unit for: / named exceptions: |
| D12 | Tests | The core's consumer tests in `tests/deploy/`, plus: |
| D13 | Packaging | The core, installed; hooks in `scripts/deploy_hooks.sh` |
| D14 | Rollout | This repo, under <ISSUE> |

